      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Hey! My friend and I are high schoolers designing a hybrid buck-boost converter on GF180 (2.7–5.5V in, 5V out, ~500mA) and want to tape out on a quarter slot. A few questions:\n\nRun 3 is too soon for us. Any idea when Run 4 will open and close, and will it have early bird pricing?\nAny student discount? We’re self-funding.\nThe COB add-on needs the default pad ring. Is there any way to get COB bonding with a custom pad ring, even for an extra fee? Our power stage needs more power pads than the default ring has.\nIf we stick with the default ring: can we turn some of the signal pads into extra power/ground pads while keeping the same bond positions, so it still works with the breakout board?\nRoughly how much current can one pad and one bond wire safely carry?\n\nThanks!",
      "author": {
        "id": "913146020798562314",
        "name": "wyomingspopulation",
        "discriminator": "0000",
